# Test: ze doctor reports a kernel with no AF_MPLS forwarding table
# Spec: plan/spec-mpls-1-kernel.md AC-6
# VALIDATES: with a BGP + fib/kernel config and no /proc/sys/net/mpls/platform_labels,
#            `ze doctor` emits doctor-mpls-unavailable so the operator learns
#            labeled routes cannot be programmed.
# Linux-only: the MPLS check lives in checks_linux.go (checks_other.go is a no-op
# elsewhere). checkMPLSSupport probes the CAPABILITY, not the module list: a
# kernel built with CONFIG_MPLS_ROUTING=y lists no mpls_router.ko and forwards
# labels anyway, which is what ze's own appliance kernel does. The probe root is
# redirected to a path that does not exist via ze.test.doctor.procfs-root, so the
# test is hermetic and does not read the host kernel it happens to run on.
#
# This config carried TWO defects that `ze doctor` accepted in silence, and
# checkBGPPeerConfig found the second one the moment the first was fixed: the
# labeled family also needs `prefix { maximum }`, which PeersFromConfigTree
# requires ("prefix maximum is mandatory and must be > 0").
#
# The peer family must be a REGISTERED labeled family: checkMPLSSupport only
# warns when mplsInUse(tree) is true, and containerPeersLabeled matches
# ipv4/ipv6 mpls-label and mpls-vpn. This test asserted against
# `ipv4/mpls-unicast`, which exists nowhere in the tree, so mplsInUse was false
# and the warning never fired. The test is skip-os everywhere but Linux, so its
# first real execution was on CI, where it failed. The invalid family also went
# unreported by `ze doctor` itself -- fixed by checkBGPPeerConfig
# (internal/component/doctor/checks_config.go), which now runs the engine's peer
# resolution and emits doctor-config-bgp-peer.

option=skip-os:value=aix,android,darwin,dragonfly,freebsd,illumos,ios,js,netbsd,openbsd,plan9,solaris,wasip1,windows
option=env:var=ze.test.doctor.procfs-root:value=proc-missing

tmpfs=mpls.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote { ip 10.0.0.2; }
			local { ip 10.0.0.1; }
		}
		session {
			asn { local 65001; remote 65002; }
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family { ipv4/mpls-label { prefix { maximum 10000; } } }
		}
	}
}
fib {
	kernel { }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json mpls.conf
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-mpls-unavailable
